<https://viewsari.ise.fiz-karlsruhe.de/ontology/#> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<https://viewsari.ise.fiz-karlsruhe.de/ontology/#> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionIRI> <https://viewsari.ise.fiz-karlsruhe.de/ontology/#/1.0.0> .
<https://viewsari.ise.fiz-karlsruhe.de/ontology/#> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#imports> <http://purl.org/spar/doco/2015-07-03> .
<https://viewsari.ise.fiz-karlsruhe.de/ontology/#> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#imports> <http://purl.org/spar/fabio/2019-02-19> .
<https://viewsari.ise.fiz-karlsruhe.de/ontology/#> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#imports> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov-o-20130430> .
<https://viewsari.ise.fiz-karlsruhe.de/ontology/#> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#imports> <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#> .
<https://viewsari.ise.fiz-karlsruhe.de/ontology/#> <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/contributor> "FIZ Karlsruhe — Leibniz Institute for Information Infrastructure, Information Service Engineering group" .
<https://viewsari.ise.fiz-karlsruhe.de/ontology/#> <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator> "Sarah Rebecca Ondraszek" .
<https://viewsari.ise.fiz-karlsruhe.de/ontology/#> <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date> "2024-01-01T09:09:00Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
<https://viewsari.ise.fiz-karlsruhe.de/ontology/#> <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/rights> "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
<https://viewsari.ise.fiz-karlsruhe.de/ontology/#> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-03-27T09:09:28Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
<https://viewsari.ise.fiz-karlsruhe.de/ontology/#> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The Viewsari ontology provides a\n        provenance-aware, FRBR-structured formal vocabulary for the\n        Viewsari knowledge graph, which models entity extraction from\n        Giorgio Vasari's Le Vite de' più eccellenti pittori, scultori,\n        e architettori (1568). It integrates the FaBiO bibliographic\n        layer, the DoCO document component vocabulary, PROV-O for\n        extraction provenance, and the W3C Web Annotation Ontology for\n        anchoring mentions to their textual evidence. The ontology\n        distinguishes three representational layers: a bibliographic\n        layer (edition, translation, volume, biography, page and their\n        web manifestations), a structural layer (paragraphs, text\n        chunks, position selectors), and a content layer (extracted\n        entities such as persons, artworks, locations, and\n        co-occurrences, together with their typed mention\n        annotations)." .
